"Restricted Disposable Income (EUR 14,469 PIL/capita): Below-average municipal income dampens discretionary beverage spending and consumption volume.", "Off-Peak Seasonal Dampening: Non-summer months (especially Winter and late Autumn) naturally reflect ~15-20% lower national beverage consumption and fewer recycling trips."], "actionable_suggestions": ["External Parking Plaza Placement: Position the RVM in the external customer parking lot near the main access road rather than in a rear store aisle. This allows car-based commuters and bulk depositors to drop 50-100 bottle bags directly from their car trunk without entering the store aisles.", "Dedicated RVM Signage & External Directional Wayfinding: Install prominent directional signage at the store entrance and customer parking lot directing shoppers directly to the Coripet recycling point. Clear visibility increases spontaneous bottle deposits by +15% to +25%.", "Institutional Community Partnerships: Connect with local schools, municipal sports centers, and environmental clubs. Designating this machine as the official collection node for school recycling competitions drives consistent, high-volume youth and family participation.", "Proactive Staff Emptying Protocol: Train store personnel to empty collection bags promptly when the 80% bin-full alert is triggered. In high-volume stores, machine-full downtime on busy Friday/Saturday afternoons permanently destroys up to 25% of potential daily volume."], "accuracy_variance_factors": ["Tourist / Commuter Corridor Effect (Potential Under-Prediction): The model\'s baseline uses permanent municipal census data (18468 inh in Marche). If this store sits on a regional tourist gateway (e.g. alpine ski/hiking routes, coastal vacation corridors, or state highways), seasonal floating foot traffic can swell actual collection volumes by +30% to +80% above permanent census projections.", "Mechanical Bin Capacity & Servicing Bottlenecks: For stores with demand exceeding ~750 bottles